      "_what": "CONTRACT v0.5/v0.8: what is SOUNDING, ~4 Hz, from SC's voices (SendReply). hz null (NaN on the wire) = silent. level = linear amplitude before the master. The page shows a pitch only from this.",
      "hz_by_layer": {
        "0": "the Tension voice's frequency (T-A or T-B, whichever SC plays)",
        "1": "the centre of the Body's dominant band (the cooked balance)",
        "2": "the Swarm's click rate, or the centre of its noise band above ~800 Hz",
        "3": "the zero-crossing frequency of the audified signal, loudest playing channel (open: Miguel; reads 3\u20135 kHz on MELH at 250\u00d7, above the \u2248 0.8 kHz spectral peak)",
        "4": "the Array: the pitch of its most excited voice (37\u2013147 Hz)",
        "5": "the Rumble: unpitched, hz NaN (level only)",
        "6": "Body v2 (as W2 defines)"
      }
    }
  },
  "transport_local": {
    "_what": "Not engine messages: how the desktop page hands the bridge a Ground ring block. The bridge sends it to scsynth as /b_setn bufnum ring_off n floats..., split so each UDP datagram stays under 64 KB. In the web build engine.js does the same /b_setn straight into the tab's scsynth.",
    "setn": {
